WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:03.200
Welcome to this short video
on how to perform intermittent

00:03.200 --> 00:07.120
catheterization with
Lofric Origo Pro.

00:07.120 --> 00:10.000
Education and training can help
you feel more confident and

00:10.000 --> 00:13.505
enable you to achieve
successful catheterization.

00:13.505 --> 00:16.705
You can use this step by step
video on how to catheterize

00:16.705 --> 00:21.825
with Lofric Origo Pro as support and
follow on from any training given.

00:21.825 --> 00:24.785
Always make sure you follow the
advice and instructions given

00:24.785 --> 00:29.720
by your clinician based on your
individual medical and lifestyle needs.

00:29.720 --> 00:33.080
First, let's briefly go through
the body parts involved in the

00:33.080 --> 00:34.520
urinary system.

00:34.520 --> 00:37.960
Your kidneys are two bean
shaped organs that clean your

00:37.960 --> 00:39.560
blood and make urine.

00:39.560 --> 00:42.840
The ureters are thin tubes that
carry urine from the kidneys

00:42.840 --> 00:44.275
down to the bladder.

00:44.275 --> 00:45.875
The bladder is a hollow,

00:45.875 --> 00:49.155
stretchy organ in your lower
belly that stores urine.

00:49.155 --> 00:52.995
The prostate is a small gland
located just below the bladder.

00:52.995 --> 00:56.035
The urethra is the tube that
carries urine from the bladder

00:56.035 --> 00:57.750
out of the body.

00:57.750 --> 01:00.870
It's completely normal to feel
a little anxious and unsure

01:00.870 --> 01:02.950
catheterizing for
the first time.

01:02.950 --> 01:05.190
Remember that for most men
who perform intermittent

01:05.190 --> 01:09.830
catheterization it's life changing
and surprisingly easy to perform.

01:09.830 --> 01:12.945
With practice and support, you
will soon become more confident.

01:12.945 --> 01:15.585
And intermittent
catheterization will become a

01:15.585 --> 01:17.745
natural part of
your daily routine.

01:17.745 --> 01:20.865
Start and end the procedure by
washing your hands thoroughly

01:20.865 --> 01:22.465
with soap and water.

01:22.465 --> 01:25.920
Hand sanitizer or wet
wipes can also be used.

01:25.920 --> 01:28.560
Remember to clean the
tip of your penis.

01:28.560 --> 01:32.560
Your clinician can advise you on
a recommended routine for this.

01:32.560 --> 01:34.080
Inside the packaging,

01:34.080 --> 01:37.200
there's a sachet with salt
solution you need to squeeze or

01:37.200 --> 01:39.440
press to release
the salt solution.

01:39.440 --> 01:42.215
The catheter is
now ready to use.

01:42.215 --> 01:44.695
Use the loop to
pull down and open.

01:44.695 --> 01:48.055
The packaging has an adhesive
tab on the reverse side,

01:48.055 --> 01:51.415
which can be used to attach
it to a dry, clean surface.

01:51.415 --> 01:55.120
Position yourself by a toilet and
pass any urine if you're able.

01:55.120 --> 01:57.520
Remove the catheter
from the package.

01:57.520 --> 02:00.320
Gently pinch and hold the
sleeve grip to automatically

02:00.320 --> 02:02.760
pull down the protective sleeve.

02:02.800 --> 02:06.080
Use your dominant hand to hold
the catheter and use your non

02:06.080 --> 02:08.205
dominant hand to
hold your penis.

02:08.205 --> 02:11.805
Lift your penis towards the
stomach to straighten the urethra.

02:11.805 --> 02:15.565
Slowly and gently insert the
catheter into the urethra,

02:15.565 --> 02:18.525
holding the catheter with
the protective sleeve.

02:18.525 --> 02:21.565
You may feel some slight
resistance as the catheter

02:21.565 --> 02:24.950
reaches your prostate area or
at the sphincter and entrance

02:24.950 --> 02:26.390
to your bladder.

02:26.390 --> 02:29.590
If you feel a little tense,
find a good position.

02:29.590 --> 02:33.430
Cough a little and
relax. Continue gently.

02:33.430 --> 02:35.270
When urine begins to flow,

02:35.270 --> 02:39.235
insert the catheter slightly
more to ensure a steady stream.

02:39.235 --> 02:43.155
Angle the penis down as urine
begins to flow through the catheter.

02:43.155 --> 02:48.275
Wait until the urine flow stops to
ensure complete bladder emptying.

02:48.275 --> 02:50.435
Slowly withdraw the catheter.

02:50.435 --> 02:53.955
The unique LoFric surface
coating will ensure that catheter is

02:53.955 --> 02:56.740
still smoothly lubricated.

02:56.740 --> 03:00.340
Put the catheter back in the
package and dispose appropriately.

03:00.340 --> 03:02.740
Local regulations may vary.

03:02.740 --> 03:05.540
Your clinician will advise
you on how often to perform

03:05.540 --> 03:08.995
intermittent catheterization
based on your conditions.

03:08.995 --> 03:11.635
This will of course depend
on factors such as how your

03:11.635 --> 03:14.995
bladder works, how often
you have to catheterize,

03:14.995 --> 03:18.355
how much you drink each
day, and other factors.

03:18.355 --> 03:22.355
Remember, LoFric Origo Pro is
a urinary catheter designed to

03:22.355 --> 03:24.520
be used only once.

03:24.520 --> 03:28.360
Did you know that LoFric Origo
Pro can easily be folded and

03:28.360 --> 03:34.040
put in your pocket so you can
take it with you wherever you go?

03:34.040 --> 03:36.520
LoFric Origo Pro
is ready for you,

03:36.520 --> 03:38.560
whatever your lifestyle needs.
